  "criteriaResults": {
    "Every mounted board-derived read filters by current board access before pagination, counts, title/body delivery, or receipt replay, including board snapshots, cards, search, My Tasks, activity, inbox, images, imports and trash.": "pass",
    "Every mounted board-derived write reauthorizes current board access in the same transaction and serializes with grant removal, including cards, comments, images, imports, columns, archive/reopen, trash and notification read state.": "pass",
    "No route silently falls back to project-only access if the board-grants migration is missing. Malformed or legacy records fail closed for non-Owners.": "pass",
    "Revoked and never-granted actors receive non-enumerating private not-found responses and cannot recover board IDs, names, titles, counts, links, assets or saved receipt data.": "pass",
    "Mounted-handler tests on isolated PostgreSQL cover Owner, Manager, Member, Viewer, no grant, revoked grant, sibling project, replay and relevant races; Node and Worker paths are reviewed.": "pass",
    "Real identity: Google callback validates state, rejects unverified or missing email_verified, never issues a session on failure, and no route issues email-only sessions in a deployed (Worker/production) runtime. dev-login is unreachable when deployed.": "pass",
    "No credential or secret has a public default outside NODE_ENV=test; /system/status, /system/migrate and existing-account dev-login are closed (403/404) without a configured secret of 32+ characters; comparison is timing-safe.": "pass",
    "Session cookies are HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure off localhost; credentialed CORS is allowed only for localhost and the explicit CORS_ORIGIN list (no wildcard hosting-domain suffixes).": "pass",
    "embedded-migrations.ts matches database/migrations/*.sql exactly, so the Worker and Node runtimes apply identical schema including board grants (0007, 0008) and additive schemas (0009, 0010).": "pass",
    "Parallel writes on one board (card create, move, and every other path that locks the board row) never deadlock into 500; deadlock/serialization failures surface as retryable errors; no lock-order inversion between project, board and grant rows is introduced.": "pass",
    "Cookie-authenticated POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE from a cross-site Origin/Referer are rejected, the origin the user sees (including behind the Pages proxy) and trusted origins still work, and no shared contract or status code changed.": "pass",
    "Current source, migrations, route files, shared helpers, contracts and tests are included in an exact manifest and a fresh independent review passes all BACKEND_REVIEW_GATE.md rules.": "pass",
    "Session tokens are stored only as a SHA-256 hash in the database; the cookie holds the raw bearer token; token lookups hash the incoming cookie; session revocation works by raw token or hash (A5/R3-10).": "pass",
    "Google OAuth sign-in preserves a user's customized display name on conflict and only updates avatar_url when a non-empty image is provided (A6/R3-11).": "pass",
    "New parity and optional fields (card key, excerpt, overdue/due-soon counters, createdBy, column tone, trash/my-tasks keys, activity card links) never leak metadata or titles to callers who lack access to the underlying board or project (A12).": "pass",
    "Migrations 0009 and 0010 are additive, idempotent, correctly backfill keys, and execute safely without data loss or table locks on existing populated tables (A13).": "pass"
  },
